<title>USA: Bids for surplus nickel range $3.0160-$3.2510/lb.</title>
<headline>Bids for surplus nickel range $3.0160-$3.2510/lb.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said Thursday it received bids from eight firms to buy surplus nickel at a price ranging from $3.0160 to $3.2510 per lb.</p>
<p>Low bidder was Keywell L.L.C. which offered to buy 80,000 lbs of nickel at $3.0160 per lb.</p>
<p>High bidder was First Miss Steel Inc which offered to buy 44,000 lbs of nickel at $3.2510 a lb.</p>
